---
import { COMPANY, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../config';
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

// Every claim here was checked against the app repository's GitHub `main` on 2026-11-25.
// Sources are listed in the phase 3 pull request. Re-check them before changing this page.
---

<Legal
  locale="en"
  path="/privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Riffu collects, why, who processes it, and how to delete it."
>
  <p>
    Riffu is an app for learning the saxophone and the clarinet. It is operated by {COMPANY.name}
    ("we"). This policy explains what the app and this website collect, why, and what you can do
    about it.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You can use Riffu without an account. Your progress then stays on your phone; the only thing
      that leaves it is an anonymous check for Pro purchases (see Purchases).
    </li>
    <li>
      The microphone is used only to find the pitch of the notes you play, on your phone or, with
      the online tuner on this website, in your browser. Sound is never recorded and never sent
      anywhere.
    </li>
    <li>
      Riffu has no ad network, no analytics and no tracking, in the app or on this website. The free
      plan shows a short break after lessons that offers Pro; it shares nothing with anyone.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you create an account, you can delete it and all of its data from the app at any time.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Without an account</h2>
  <p>
    Your progress, settings and practice history are stored only on your phone. We do not receive
    them. Deleting the app deletes them.
  </p>

  <h2>With an account</h2>
  <p>
    An account lets you keep your progress and Pro when you change phones. You sign in with a
    one-time code sent to your email, or with Sign in with Apple. With an account, we store:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your email address</strong>, to sign you in. With Sign in with Apple, this can be the
      private relay address Apple creates for you, and we also receive the identifier Apple uses for
      you in Riffu.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your name</strong>, only if you share it through Sign in with Apple.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your course progress:</strong> your instrument, the lessons you finished, your XP, the
      days you practised and your streak, your daily goal, your beats, and the questions waiting for
      you to review. It also holds an identifier that the app creates for each phone, so progress
      from two phones can be merged.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A token from Apple</strong>, if you use Sign in with Apple. We keep it only so we can
      ask Apple to remove Riffu's access when you delete your account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sign-in records</strong>: when you signed in and the IP address used, kept by our
      database provider for security.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your practice minutes, the notes you missed and your tuner readings stay on your phone. We use
    the data above only to run Riffu for you: to sign you in, keep your progress, and give you Pro.
    We do not sell it, share it for advertising, or use it to build a profile of you.
  </p>

  <h2>The microphone</h2>
  <p>
    Riffu asks for the microphone so it can hear your instrument. The sound is analysed on your
    phone to find the pitch of each note. It is never recorded to a file and never sent to us or
    anyone else. You can turn the microphone off for Riffu in your phone's settings; the tuner and
    the lessons that listen will then not work.
  </p>

  <h2>The online tuner</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/tuner">tuner on this website</a> asks your browser for the microphone only when
    you press Start tuner. The sound is analysed in your browser, on your own device, to find the
    pitch of the note you play. It is never recorded, never stored and never sent to us or anyone
    else: the page sends no requests while it listens, and it saves nothing, not even your
    instrument or your tuning reference. The microphone is released when you stop the tuner, switch
    to another tab or leave the page. You can block the microphone for this website in your
    browser's settings at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Notifications</h2>
  <p>
    If you turn on the daily practice reminder, your phone schedules it. No notification token is
    sent to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Pro is sold through the App Store and needs a Riffu account. Apple handles the payment; we never
    see your card details. We use RevenueCat to manage subscriptions. When Riffu opens, it asks
    RevenueCat whether you have Pro: without an account it uses an anonymous identifier created on
    your phone, and with an account it uses your Riffu account identifier. RevenueCat receives that
    identifier, your purchase history, basic information about your device and app version, and your
    IP address.
  </p>

  <h2>Who processes your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Supabase</strong> stores your account and its data, on servers in the United States.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Resend</strong> sends the one-time sign-in codes, so it receives your email address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Apple</strong>, for Sign in with Apple and App Store purchases.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>RevenueCat</strong>, for subscriptions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Vercel</strong> hosts this website. To deliver its pages, it processes your IP address
      and may keep it in short-lived server logs.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each processes data only to provide its service to us. If you live outside the United States,
    your data is transferred to and processed in the United States.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking. Its fonts and images are served
    from this site, not from third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your account data until you delete your account. When you delete it, we delete your
    account and every row of its data straight away. Copies may remain in our providers' backups for
    a limited time until they are overwritten. Apple and RevenueCat keep their own records of
    purchases, under their own policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Delete:</strong> delete your account in the app, or follow
      <a href="/delete-account">Delete your account</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Access, correct or export:</strong> write to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> from your account's email address, and
      we will answer within 30 days.
    </li>
    <li>
      Depending on where you live, you may have more rights, such as objecting to processing or
      complaining to your data protection authority. Write to us and we will help.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Riffu is for people 13 and over. It is not directed to children under 13, and we do not
    knowingly collect their data. Where local law sets a higher age for agreeing to data processing
    (for example 14 in Spain), that age applies, and a younger learner needs a parent's or
    guardian's consent. If you believe a child under 13 has an account, write to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If what Riffu collects changes, we update this page before that version of the app ships, and
    change the date at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <address>
    {COMPANY.name}
    <br />
    {COMPANY.address}
    <br />
    <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
  </address>
</Legal>
